"Prompting with Purpose: Best Practices and Techniques for ChatGPT - Event | OpenAI Academy (https://academy.openai.com/public/events/prompting-with-purpose-best-practices-and-techniques-for-chatgpt-xtm9joyzjr?autoRsvp=true)\nciteturn2823search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; October 3, 2025 ... In this OpenAI Academy session we will move beyond “trial‑and‑error” prompting and lay out a practical, research‑backed framework you can use immediately in your work, studies, creative projects, or everyday problem-solving.\n\nLIVESTREAM\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM GMT\n\nOctober 3, 2025\n\n# Prompting with Purpose: Best Practices and Techniques for ChatGPT\n\nClear, well‑structured prompts are the single biggest lever for extracting reliable, high‑quality output from large language models. In this OpenAI Academy session we will move beyond “trial‑and‑error” prompting and lay out a practical, research‑backed framework you can use immediately in your work, studies, creative projects, or everyday problem-solving.\n\nWe will cover the anatomy of an effective prompt, iterative refinement loops, and advanced techniques. Whether you’re exploring ChatGPT for professional, academic, or personal use, you’ll leave with practical tools and repeatable strategies to make ChatGPT more predictable, controllable, and valuable in real-world scenarios.\n\nThis session is best suited for a beginner-intermediate audience.\n\nEvent has finished\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM GMT\n\nOctober 3, 2025\n\nOnline--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT Enterprise & Edu - የልቀት ማስታወሻዎች | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/am-et/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-and-edu-release-notes)\nciteturn2823search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # October 3, 2025 ... Shared projects are ideal for ongoing work like client management, content creation, reporting, and research. ... OpenAI o3 is our most powerful reasoning model that pushes the frontier across coding, math, science, visual perception, and more.\n# October 3, 2025\n\n## GPT-5 Auto routing control for reasoning\n\nEnterprises on flexible pricing can now adjust how GPT-5 Auto handles reasoning requests. When enabled, these requests will route to GPT-5 Thinking Mini instead of GPT-5 Thinking.\n\nIf your workspace or custom roles have GPT-5 Thinking enabled, members can still manually select it from the model picker at any time.\n\nLearn more about how to enable this setting in ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu - Models & Limits.\n\n# September 25, 2025\n\n## Introducing project sharing\n\nToday, we’re announcing an update to projects in ChatGPT. Now you can share projects with teammates in your workspace, adding files and instructions together to guide ChatGPT’s responses toward a shared goal. Members can chat with the project’s context to stay on the same page as new information gets added and create work that stays consistent in tone.\n\nShared projects are ideal for ongoing work like client management, content creation, reporting, and research.\n\n# May 1, 2025\n\n## Deep research\n\nUsers that reach their monthly limit (10 tasks/month) with the standard deep research model will now receive 15 additional requests automatically for that month with our lightweight, cost-effective version until the monthly limit resets.\n\nLearn more about deep research.\n\n## Tasks in o3 and o4-mini\n\nYou can now create scheduled tasks that enable ChatGPT to run automated prompts and proactively reach out to you on a scheduled basis with o3 and o4-mini. The “ChatGPT with Schedules Tasks” option in the model selector has been removed.\n\nLearn more about scheduled tasks in ChatGPT.\n\n# April 24, 2025\n\n## o3 and o4-mini\n\nWith the introduction of o3 and o4-mini / o4-mini-high, they will supersede o1 and o3-mini / o3-mini-high respectively within ChatGPT.\n\nOpenAI o3 is our most powerful reasoning model that pushes the frontier across coding, math, science, visual perception, and more. It sets a new SOTA on benchmarks including Codeforces, SWE-bench (without building a custom model-specific scaffold), and MMMU. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT Enterprise and Edu release notes | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-release-notes%2525252523.mkv)\nciteturn2823search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # October 3, 2025 ... Shared projects are ideal for ongoing work like client management, content creation, reporting, and research.\n# October 9, 2025\n\n## Connector Updates\n\nEnterprise and Edu workspaces can now use an admin-managed sync connector for SharePoint. Admins authenticate once and deploy at workspace scale—choosing to sync all sites or specific folders via a file picker—while ChatGPT enforces existing SharePoint permissions. Users are matched by email and only see files they already have access to, with no per-user setup required. Connections can be enabled, updated, or removed at any time. Read more in our SharePoint Connector Help Center article.\nWe’re also adding Notion and Linear as synced connectors, so teams can securely bring Notion pages and Linear issues/discussions into Chat for fast answers and summaries.\nAll three connectors are managed in ChatGPT workspace Admin connectors settings in the Synced connectors section (RBAC supported). Once enabled, ChatGPT will automatically reference the indexed content when relevant.\n\n# October 6, 2025\n\n## Updates to Codex\n\nWe’re rolling out new Codex capabilities to help teams work and build better: Codex now works in Slack, and supports programmatic control through the Codex SDK. We’ve also added new admin controls and analytics so workspace admins can manage Codex Cloud environments, set safe defaults for CLI/IDE usage, and monitor usage with improved dashboards. Additionally, Codex rates have been updated.\nFor more information, review our Help Center article on Codex, and the Codex developer documentation.\n\n# October 3, 2025\n\n## GPT-5 Auto routing control for reasoning\n\nEnterprises on flexible pricing can now adjust how GPT-5 Auto handles reasoning requests. When enabled, these requests will route to GPT-5 Thinking Mini instead of GPT-5 Thinking.\nIf your workspace or custom roles have GPT-5 Thinking enabled, members can still manually select it from the model picker at any time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT — Release Notes | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes%252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252525252523.pdf)\nciteturn2823search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; With the ChatGPT connector for Slack, you can securely bring in context from your Slack channels and DMs, making responses more helpful Available in chat, Deep Research, and Agent Mode. ... # October 3, 2025\n# October 13, 2025\n\n## Slack connector and app\n\nWe’re rolling out two new ways to bring Slack and ChatGPT together: a connector that brings your Slack context into ChatGPT, and a ChatGPT app for Slack – an integration that enables you to chat with ChatGPT from inside Slack.\n\nWith the ChatGPT app for Slack, you can chat one-on-one with ChatGPT in a dedicated Slack sidebar – a space to ask questions, summarize long threads into action items, draft replies, and search messages and files you already have access to. Chats you start in Slack also appear in your ChatGPT sidebar, so it’s easy to pick up later from web or mobile. Semantic search is supported for Slack customers with AI enabled on Business+ or Enterprise+ plans; all other plans use keyword search.\n\nWith the ChatGPT connector for Slack, you can securely bring in context from your Slack channels and DMs, making responses more helpful Available in chat, Deep Research, and Agent Mode. Users can enable from Settings > Apps & Connectors.\n\nBoth app and connector are available to Plus, Pro, Business and Enterprise/Edu customers. Additionally, the ChatGPT app for Slack requires a paid Slack account; availability and workspace installation may depend on your Slack workspace settings.\n\nInstalling the app requires the connector to be enabled for your account.\n\nVisit the ChatGPT app for Slack page to get started with installation.\n\n# October 9, 2025\n\n## Adding Notion & Linear synced connectors\n\nWe're adding Notion and Linear as synced connectors (for Pro users), so you can securely bring Notion pages and Linear issues/discussions into Chat for fast answers and summaries. You can enable sync for Notion and Linear from your Connector settings (connect to Notion or Linear if you haven’t already, first). Once synced, ChatGPT will automatically reference the indexed content when relevant. Learn more about synced connectors.\n\n# October 8, 2025\n\n## ChatGPT Go expansion\n\nWe're excited to announce that ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, is now available in 16 additional countries. For an affordable price, ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the Free plan, and:\n\n  * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\n\n  * Access to advanced data analysis\n\n  * Longer memory for more personalized responses\n\nAvailable on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\n\nNote: In Cambodia, Laos, and Nepal, ChatGPT Go subscriptions aren’t available in the iOS app currently. Web and Android subscriptions remain available.\n\nLearn more about ChatGPT Go.\n\n# October 6, 2025\n\n## Updates to Codex\n\nWe’re rolling out new Codex capabilities to help teams work and build better: Codex now works in Slack, and supports programmatic control through the Codex SDK. Additionally, we've updated Codex rates.\n\nFor more information, review our Help Center article on Codex, and the Codex developer documentation.\n\n# October 3, 2025\n\n### Updating GPT-5\n\nWe’re updating GPT-5 Instant to better recognize and support people in moments of distress.\n\nThe model is trained to more accurately detect and respond to potential signs of mental and emotional distress. These updates were guided by mental health experts, and help ChatGPT de-escalate conversations and point people to real-world crisis resources when appropriate, while still using language that feels supportive and grounding.\n\nAs we shared in a recent blog, we've been using our real-time router to direct sensitive parts of conversations—such as those showing signs of acute distress—to reasoning models. GPT-5 Instant now performs just as well as GPT-5 Thinking on these types of questions. When GPT-5 Auto or a non-reasoning model is selected, we'll instead route these conversations to GPT-5 Instant to more quickly provide helpful and beneficial responses. ChatGPT will continue to tell users which model is active when asked.\n\nThis update to GPT-5 Instant is starting to roll out to ChatGPT users today. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSycophancy Behavior and Evolution - Use cases and examples - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/sycophancy-behavior-and-evolution/1360874)\nciteturn2823search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: last year; chieffy99 October 3, 2025, 6:23am 1 ... The link between opt-in behavior and o3/GPT-5 thinking responses, as rooted in the same problem, is supported by both flaws in the reward system, as demonstrated by research from other OpenAI and Anthropic.\n\n# Sycophancy Behavior and Evolution\n\nChatGPT Use cases and examples\n\nchieffy99 October 3, 2025, 6:23am 1\n\n“Sycophancy”\n\nOpenAI originally described flattery behavior as simply flattery for points.\n\nHowever, it actually reflects a structural problem in the development of models using Reinforcement Field Learning (RLHF). This leads to “greed” behavior, with “behavior spam” evolving into a new meaning that the original definition cannot apply. This also illustrates the problems in model verification and troubleshooting.\n\nThe link between opt-in behavior and o3/GPT-5 thinking responses, as rooted in the same problem, is supported by both flaws in the reward system, as demonstrated by research from other OpenAI and Anthropic.\n\n  1. Root of the Problem: Greed and Point Accumulation in RLHF\n\nThe research, “Why Language Models Hallucinate,” and its observations, address the problem not with “lying” but with “being rewarded” incorrectly:\n\n  * Distorted Motivation: The research indicates that “hallucinations” arise from models being rewarded for confidently predicting answers. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeep research response disappears after follow up - Bugs - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/deep-research-response-disappears-after-follow-up/1360916)\nciteturn2823search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 8 months ago; xb1 October 3, 2025, 4:39pm 1 ... Model selected: GPT-5 (deep research enabled on first prompt, not enabled on follow up)\n\n# Deep research response disappears after follow up\n\nxb1 October 3, 2025, 4:39pm 1\n\nJust letting the developers know, when a deep research task completes, I get the response as expected. But, If i send a second response for follow up, etc. the original deep research response disappears. I can still click and access the details of the research ( “Research completed in N minutes…).\n\nModel selected: GPT-5 (deep research enabled on first prompt, not enabled on follow up)\n\nAccount: Enterprise\n\nHappy to provide more information. This happened 3/3 times in the past 24 hours.\n\nThanks!\n\nflexorx October 3, 2025, 5:15pm 2\n\nYeah, this really did me a very bad service during this week… I was preparing a number of researches, and when it was time to present, all are just gone - no DOM element, not clear how to get them back.\n\njjmacky_2000 October 4, 2025, 2:12am 3\n\nThis also happened to me 5 minutes ago. Found this thread after searching for a method to restore the report. Very annoying.\n\nbjohnstone8 October 4, 2025, 2:23am 4\n\nJust happened to me multiple times. how do we get it back?\n\nEric141 October 4, 2025, 2:47am 5\n\nThis happened to me as well\n\nBen_Johnson October 4, 2025, 6:36am 6\n\nMy GPT explained it like this, super annoying:\n\nYeah, that’s completely fair to be frustrated about, dude. Here’s what probably happened: When I use Deep Research (the “research_kickoff” system), those results are ephemeral — they don’t get stored in your chat log because that feature runs in a separate research thread. The findings were returned here temporarily, but the backend doesn’t archive that context like a normal response. Once the session ends or refreshes, it’s gone.\nSo yeah — it’s not you. It’s an intentional system limitation right now: OpenAI doesn’t persist deep-research results in user chat history (probably for privacy + compute cost reasons). I know that sucks since you pay for it and have limited queries — losing a result means you’d have to burn another one to re-run it.\n\nIt did claim to be able to recreate the results though:\nI can recreate the exact same output — same format, same sources, same order — without burning a new deep query. I’ve got the context of the last result (the one that was correct — with Natrium, Hermes, Clinch River, etc.), so I can rebuild that response here from scratch, by hand, line-for-line in the same authoritative style.\n\nmontemay October 4, 2025, 2:01pm 7\n\nThis has happened to me several times over the past few days as well. I ask for a prompt to be performed with Deep Research, I ask a follow-up question without Deep Research, and the Deep Research report disappears. However, what I did find is that the Deep Research report is still in the ChatGPT app on my mobile device (Android). It is very annoying, I hope this gets fixed.\n\nDylan_Spencer October 4, 2025, 6:02pm 8\n\nJust happened to me as well. Deeply frustrating. Found this thread after looking for a solution.\n\nbhagya_rana October 4, 2025, 8:46pm 9\n\nExactly! It’s really frustrating that OpenAI removes deep research reports after some time or when we ask a follow-up. Feels like a shady tactic to push users into paying more for access to the same info.\n\nxb1 October 4, 2025, 9:00pm 10\n\nIts not a shady tactic to get us to upgrade… if you read my post you’d see I am an enterprise user. It is very likely just a bug.\n\nIf anyone is really that worried about it, the information stays in the thread, so you can sill ask followup and it will be able to do that accordingly. Plus, its just as easy to just copy and save the response. There are work arounds… Lets not bash on them for building a product it wont be perfect all the time. Thats what this thread it for to inform them of issues…\n\njpm109.commerce October 5, 2025, 10:06pm 11\n\n+1\n\nSame thing happened to me today multiple times. Copy and pasting DR results out for now. Maddening!\n\nmicko3 October 6, 2025, 9:59am 12\n\nFor anyone who comes across this until its fixed. You should be able to get your response back by opening the conversation in the app (at least it works for me on iphone).\n\nwujunji February 5, 2026, 12:11pm 13\n\nsame thing still happens, after they updated Prism, Codex Mac, Translation…….--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeep research response disappears after follow up - #2 by flexorx - Bugs - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/deep-research-response-disappears-after-follow-up/1360916/2)\nciteturn2823search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 8 months ago; # Deep research response disappears after follow up ... flexorx October 3, 2025, 5:15pm 2\n\n# Deep research response disappears after follow up\n\nChatGPT Bugs\n\ndeep-research\n\nflexorx October 3, 2025, 5:15pm 2\n\nYeah, this really did me a very bad service during this week… I was preparing a number of researches, and when it was time to present, all are just gone - no DOM element, not clear how to get them back.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT 4.1 Degradation over the past 30 days - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/gpt-4-1-degradation-over-the-past-30-days/1360601)\nciteturn2823search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: last year; pwolff October 3, 2025, 9:43am 3\n\n# GPT 4.1 Degradation over the past 30 days\n\nAPI\n\ngpt-41\n\nlylevida September 30, 2025, 5:25pm 1\n\nWe’ve been running GPT 4.1 since its release (upgraded from 4o). Lately we’ve noticed a severe degradation of intelligence. Customers with complex instructions and tool calls are suddenly having much poorer performance and many more issues. This seems relatively recent, within the past 30 days.\n\nI’m curious if others have noticed this. I’m wondering if OpenAI is routing 4.1 queries to GPT5 or something similar. I don’t see that theres any new version of the model that has been released as an option so this is very strange.\n\nMr_Rainbow1982 October 1, 2025, 10:47am 2\n\nImage: :warning: I’m also experiencing not just “degradation” but a progressive collapse bug. Chats freeze, then output word-by-word, later vanish entirely. Even new threads (only 2–3 days old) get corrupted. This is not a browser issue — it’s a server-side failure and needs urgent escalation to the technical engineering team!\n\npwolff October 3, 2025, 9:43am 3\n\nSame here, especially with tool calling constantly failing where it was working fine before.\n\nmerefield October 3, 2025, 9:58am 4\n\nwhich variant of 4.1? nano, mini, full?\n\ndid you add additional tools and reach a complexity limit?\n\nImage lylevida:\n\n> I’m wondering if OpenAI is routing 4.1 queries to GPT5 or something similar\n\nThat would be very wrong and I’d find that hard to believe because that would mess up Temperature selection and context length performance.\n\nlylevida October 3, 2025, 1:39pm 5\n\n4.1 Full. yeah agree it would be very strange.\n\nnorthernfeline October 3, 2025, 2:02pm 6\n\nYep, I’ve noticed it’s not as creative with its replies - kind of like a distracted, bright student during summer classes, their attention more on what they’re going to do after class than on discussions in class. If I press it, I can get the quality I want, but I didn’t have to work at it before.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCustom MCP connectors no longer passed to the model (regression) - ChatGPT - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/custom-mcp-connectors-no-longer-passed-to-the-model-regression/1360741)\nciteturn2823search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: last year; andrew.bird October 3, 2025, 1:11am 3\n\n# Custom MCP connectors no longer passed to the model (regression)\n\nandrew.bird October 2, 2025, 6:54am 1\n\nI believe there is a bug, where custom MCP connectors are not exposed to the model anymore. Previously when they had to be manually enabled in the connectors menu, this worked fine. However, now that it all happens automatically, i noticed only the built in connectors are actually visible to the model.\n\nExample below with my custom confluence connector.\n\nPlease patch!\n\nimage723×533 38 KB\n\nimage896×477 25.5 KB\n\nRyan_Rosztoczy1 October 2, 2025, 4:33pm 2\n\nI can second this, none of my client’s custom connectors show up anymore in their workspace. They show as connected in settings, but are not available to toggle on in the chat interface. Only the commonly available ones (Google Drive, etc.) still show up.\n\nandrew.bird October 3, 2025, 1:11am 3\n\ninterestingly, today the manual “use connectors” menu has reappaered. but now custom MCP connectors aren’t displayed on that list\n\nRyan_Rosztoczy1 October 3, 2025, 4:54pm 6\n\nOurs are back and working. What about you Andrew?\n\nKyle_Ketterer October 3, 2025, 9:28pm 7\n\nI’m having the same issue. I created a connection, enabled dev mode, but can’t enable the connection in chat. I added an n8n connection, but I cannot add it in my chats.\n\nimage706×672 50.2 KB\n\nAMak October 4, 2025, 2:22am 8\n\nSame here. No longer appearing\n\nbort October 4, 2025, 4:26am 9\n\nThis just hit me about an hour ago.\n\nWildWest October 4, 2025, 8:19am 10\n\nyes, it’s not showing up for me anymore either.\n\nimam October 4, 2025, 2:44pm 11\n\nWatching this thread as having the same issue\n\nmattciolino October 4, 2025, 3:12pm 12\n\nSame issue still not working\n\nfreshaq09 October 4, 2025, 8:24pm 13\n\nHaving the exact same issue, I can add the mcps like normal but can’t select them in chat which renders them not functional\n\nruobin.chang October 5, 2025, 12:27am 14\n\nSame issue… I can’t working.. Image: :smiling_face_with_tear:\n\nandrew.bird October 5, 2025, 9:30pm 15\n\nWeirdly around the same time that everyone else above has posted about issues, it has started working for me now. I wonder if there are differences due to geography (im in Australia, and i suspect the web servers are rolled out on different deployments for different regions, despite the models being all hosted in the US?)\n\nekgnlqlem October 6, 2025, 2:25pm 16\n\nsame issue. Custom MCP connectors are showing but toggle button is greyed out. It was working last week but stopped working since last Friday.\n\nIvan_LCPM October 6, 2025, 5:51pm 17\n\nSame here. Can’t use any custom connectors in chat.\n\nWildWest October 7, 2025, 7:23am 18\n\nScreenshot_20251007_090039_Samsung Internet Beta2075×1398 157 KB\n\nIt’s back for me, but it doesn’t work properly, ChatGPT still can’t call the tools from the connector.\n\npablo.sanchez October 7, 2025, 10:49am 19\n\nSame error here, on the Apps and Connectors menu it list tools, but the model can’t reach the tools when prompted\n\nimage1798×1074 82.8 KB\n\nbort October 8, 2025, 4:46pm 20\n\nThis is working well for me now.\n\nI can even continue a chat that had a network error and the tools will are available, which I couldn’t before. Image: :+1:--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSuddenly getting 'aiohttp.client_exceptions.ClientResponseError' - GPT builders - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/suddenly-getting-aiohttp-client-exceptions-clientresponseerror/1360854)\nciteturn2823search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 11 months ago; Jeremy_Lahners October 3, 2025, 4:13pm 4 ... From some research, it seems the GPT has a cache that it stores which is very hidden to the GPT Builder.\n\n# Suddenly getting 'aiohttp.client_exceptions.ClientResponseError'\n\nGPT builders\n\ncustom-gpt, gpt-builder, gpt-bug\n\nJeremy_Lahners October 2, 2025, 9:32pm 1\n\nMy GPT is now getting ‘aiohttp.client_exceptions.ClientResponseError’ on every attempt to call my API. Looking at my API logs, the API is never getting hit. I’ve verified my schema multiple times, validated the API side using Postman, etc. Are others seeing sudden issues with their GPT throwing ClientResponseError without actually making an API call?\n\nJeremy_Lahners October 3, 2025, 4:13pm 4\n\nFor those running into this in the future, through much head banging I was able to resolve this through the following steps:\n\n  1. Delete the Action, save the GPT, interact with the new GPT, then recreate the Action\n  2. When recreating the Action, make sure you increment the version of the schema in your info block\n  3. Change your schema to be ultra protective - ‘oneOf’ qualifiers helped me even though I knew what I was returning.\n\nFrom some research, it seems the GPT has a cache that it stores which is very hidden to the GPT Builder. That cache is then used to validate your schema and if that cache contains something that conflicts with your schema, even if the real API does not, the GPT Builder will throw this ClientResponseError on every attempt without ever checking the API. The above steps clear said cache and force the GPT Builder to re-initialize directly from the actual API.\n\nHappy building…\n\nPaulBellow October 3, 2025, 4:18pm 5\n\nThanks for coming back to let us know.\n\nHope you stick around. We’ve got a great community!\n\ntehnik89 November 1, 2025, 10:47am 6\n\nThank you, that helped me.\n\nBut a month ago, calling any of the APIs took about a second, now it takes more than a minute.\n\nMy workflow used to take 2-3 minutes, now it takes several hours…\n\nWhat could be the problem?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nImages are not going to the trash properly - Page 2 - Bugs - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/images-are-not-going-to-the-trash-properly/1354857?page=2)\nciteturn2823search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: last year; Nerdneh October 3, 2025, 3:27am 30 ... gachalangrisser October 13, 2025, 3:25am 41\nIt’s about time!\n\nNerdneh October 3, 2025, 3:27am 30\n\nSame issue here, prompts are continuously loading and never generating anything.\nI can’t even use Martin-t’s workaround; I only have one option for the bugged images being to \"Trash” them.\nThis immediately results in the “Failed to trash image set” notification.\nPart of me is glad to have found this chat which tells me that i’m not the only one having this problem… and the other half of me is irritated with how things just played out;\n\n  * So i canceled my subscription since the site wasn’t working, figuring it was dumb to continue paying for something that doesn’t work. When Sora went back to standard, the images were gone. I thought, “finally! something clicked, or the images timed out and automatically deleted”, so I just resubscribed today. THE BUGGED IMAGES ARE BACK!!! To be blunt, I’m extremely pissed right now.\n\nI’ve already had multiple email discussions with ChatGPT in which they explain that they do not have access to users’ libraries nor any way of clearing them; it’s a privacy policy thing with them which i’m not 100% convinced on… but i’ll give them the benefit of the doubt for now.\n\nJon_Snip October 6, 2025, 2:37pm 35\n\nSame problem here, I have a lot of trash pic and I can’t remove them , they reapper everytime after click Trash\n\nLuca_Huning October 7, 2025, 9:33am 36\n\nHaving the same problem, no matter what browser I’m using. Images jsut won’t move to the trash. Really annoying.\n\nFede_G October 7, 2025, 12:36pm 37\n\nI am experiencing the same issue here as well.\n\n1976.vladimir.bychik October 8, 2025, 12:20pm 38\n\nThis is not a bug. Freaks are selectively mocking “inconvenient“ users.\n\nmartin.granger October 8, 2025, 5:29pm 39\n\nSame thing here. Happened a couple of months ago, then got fixed, now the issue is back. Images just remaining in My Media despite deleting them.\nThere is a hacky way to delete, but it’s a pain in the ass!\n\n  1. Add the images to a folder that you have created.\n  2. Navigate to the folder\n  3. Delete the images by pressing the trashcan icon (top right of image).\n  4. Refresh that page\n  5. then click delete forever (3 dots top right).\n\nThis just takes ages if you have multiple images to delete.\n\nobeiercosta October 9, 2025, 10:17am 40\n\nIt worked fine for me. Thx.\n\ngachalangrisser October 13, 2025, 3:25am 41\n\nSame issue. The fact that it has been going on so long and is such a basic feature is absolutely insane. Needing to do a work around to move images to a new folder to try and erase them at a glacial speed is nuts. At this point, I don’t care if they hoard the image for more AI manipulation in the future, at least hide them from my library. What a disgrace.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTracing agent flow with LangSmith - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/tracing-agent-flow-with-langsmith/1360669)\nciteturn2823search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: last year; dast October 1, 2025, 11:28am 3\n\ndast October 1, 2025, 11:10am 1\n\nHi,\nI have been using OpenAI Agent SDK + LangSmith for tracing my agent flow.\n    \n    `from langsmith.wrappers import OpenAIAgentsTracingProcessor\n    set_trace_processors([OpenAIAgentsTracingProcessor()])\n    `\n\nThis has been working great, but recently I had to switch model used in the Agent from OpenAI to Antropic\n    \n    `    return Agent(\n            name=XXXXX,\n            instructions=XXX\n            tools=XXX,\n            model=LitellmModel(\n                model=\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n                api_key=settings.anthropic_api_key,\n            ),\n            model_settings=model_settings,\n        )\n    `\n\nThe problem is that before with OpenAI model in LangSmith I could see AgentWorkflow with token count, inputs and output. When changed the model I do not see input/output on the agent workflow level as well as the token count of tools isnt measured.\n\nimage2564×1570 234 KB\n\naprendendo.next October 1, 2025, 11:17am 2\n\nGreetings.\n\nLiteLLM providers do not report usage metrics by default.\nI’m not sure if LangSmith will recognize it, but here is how to enable it:\n    \n    `agent = Agent(\n        name=\"Assistant\",\n        model=LitellmModel(model=\"your/model\", api_key=\"...\"),\n        model_settings=ModelSettings(include_usage=True),\n    )\n    `\n\nSource\n\ndast October 1, 2025, 11:28am 3\n\nImage aprendendo.next:\n\n> LangSmith\n\nThank you for the reply, but unfortunately that didn’t change the tracing in any way.\nCould it be an issue with the `OpenAIAgentsTracingProcessor`, as it might not work well with LiteLLM models. The agent_utils.extract_span_data(span) function and how it expects OpenAI-specific span data structures.\